      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1900 a railway station at Notre Dame Junction six miles south helped turn Lewisporte into a shipping hub for Timber Estates Limited sawmill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lewisporte.ca/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During WWII, Lewisporte hosted three army sites protecting oil supply lines to Gander, later disappearing after rapid postwar growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
